    "lawCode": "Amd §2.10, CP L",
    "lawSection": "Criminal Procedure Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S2940\n\n\n\npURPOSE: This legislation grants peace officer statns to unifonned\nconrt officers employed by\n\nthe village of Northport justice court.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS : Section 2.10 ofthe criminal procedure law is\namended by adding a new subdivision 83 to grant peace officer status\nto uniformed court officers for the village of Northport justice\ncourt.\n\n JUSTIFICATION : The Northport Village Justice Court is the local\ncriminal court in which all the accusatory instruments of the\nNorthport police Department are filed. The court has regularly\nscheduled hours every Monday from 6:00 P.M. until the docket is\ncomplete. The court also arraigns defendants during non-traditional\nhours and has held jury and non-jury trials during traditional\nbusiness hours. The Northport Police Department has been providing\ncourtroom security for the Northport Village Justice Court for more\nthan 100 years. Unfortunately, because of decreasing personnel the\nDepartment is unable to staff the court with police officers.\n\nThe Chief of Police has at his disposal, several qualified individuals\nwho would make excellent court officers for the available part time\nwork. All of these individuals are recently retired police officers.\nBecause of Suffolk County Civil Service regulations they cannot\nmaintain their police officer status working for the court, but they\nhave the requisites to be peace officers. With appro:al of this\nlegislation, the court can be assured of a safe and professional\natmosphere during the miscellaneous hours when it is necessary to\nprovide staff for the Court.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY : S.6545/A.l0397, Vetoed.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS : None.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE : This act shall take effect immediately.\n",
